#      1:     11: ! * Automated test for the network library. It is the Pascaline equivalent of  *
#      1:     12: ! * the Ami network_test.c reference test: each of the manual tests (gettys/   *
#      1:     13: ! * telnet, msgserver/msgclient, prtcertnet, plain and secure) is run          *
#      1:     14: ! * automatically against a loopback server, so no external server and no      *
#      1:     15: ! * second console is needed.                                                  *
#      1:     16: ! *                                                                             *
#      1:     17: ! * The tests:                                                                 *
#      1:     18: ! *                                                                             *
#      1:     19: ! * 1. addrnet: name lookup of localhost gives the loopback address.           *
#      1:     20: ! * 2. TCP connection in the clear: server waitnet, client opennet, a line     *
#      1:     21: ! *    exchanged in each direction (the gettys/telnet test automated).         *
#      1:     22: ! * 3. TCP connection secured (TLS): the same exchange with secure on.         *
#      1:     23: ! * 4. Messages in the clear: server waitmsg, client openmsg, a message        *
#      1:     24: ! *    exchanged in each direction (the msgserver/msgclient test automated).   *
#      1:     25: ! * 5. Messages secured (DTLS): the same exchange with secure on.              *
#      1:     26: ! * 6. maxmsg/relymsg: sanity of the message limits for the loopback address.  *
#      1:     27: ! * 7. certnet: the raw certificate of the secure server is retrievable and    *
#      1:     28: ! *    non-empty (the prtcertnet test automated against our own server).       *
#      1:     29: ! *                                                                             *
#      1:     30: ! * Pascaline has no fork, so the loopback servers are self-spawned server     *
#      1:     31: ! * roles: with an empty command line the program runs the test suite, and for *
#      1:     32: ! * each test needing a server it spawns itself again (services exec) with a   *
#      1:     33: ! * role command line, 'tcpserver <port> <secure>' or 'msgserver <port>        *
#      1:     34: ! * <secure>'. The server role serves exactly one client, then exits.          *
#      1:     35: ! *                                                                             *
#      1:     36: ! * The decoded certificate list (certlistnet) is not tested: per the note in  *
#      1:     37: ! * network_test.txt, that decode path is not completely working yet.          *
